      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg,\n\nThanks for your review. The following snippet describes how we use the three functions.\n\n1. Create a device class by:\nsome_class \u003d class_create(THIS_MODULE, SOME_CLASS_NAME);\n\n2. Create a device (struct device) by:\nstruct mtk_defined_drvdata *drv_data;\ndevice_create(some_class, parent_dev, dev_number, drv_data, \"%s\", some_name);\n\n3.After we get a buntch of devices under this class, we could iterate the class and search the drv_data we need by:\n\nstruct device *dev;\nstruct class_dev_iter iter;\nstruct mtk_defined_drvdata *drv_data;\n\nclass_dev_iter_init(\u0026iter, some_class, NULL, NULL);\nwhile((dev \u003d class_dev_iter_next(\u0026iter)) \u0026\u0026 some_condition) {\n\tdrv_data \u003d dev_get_drvdata(dev);\n\tdo_sth_on(drv_data);\n}\n\nclass_dev_iter_exit(\u0026iter);",
